      "text": " .\n\n**Final Answer**.\nThe product of 53 and 24 is \\boxed{1272}.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\nTo find the product of 53 and 24:\n\n1. **Break down using distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   53 \\times 24 = (50 + 3) \\times (20 + 4)\n   \\]\n   Expand the terms:\n   \\[\n   = 50 \\times 20 + 50 \\times 4 + 3 \\times 20 + 3 \\times 4\n   \\]\n   Calculate each part:\n   \\[\n   = 1000 + 200 + 60 + 12 = 1272\n   \\]\n\n2. **Standard multiplication algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 53 by 4:\n     \\[\n     53 \\times 4 = 212\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 53 by 20 (shift one place left):\n     \\[\n     53 \\times 20 = 1060\n     \\]\n   - Add the partial products:\n     \\[\n     212 + 1060 = 1272\n     \\]\n\n3. **Verification via division:**\n   - Divide the result by 53:\n     \\[\n     1272 \\div 53 = 24\n     \\]\n   - Divide the result by 24:\n     \\[\n     1272 \\div 24 = 53\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{1272}\\).",
