      "text": "9934.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 69 and 86 is \\boxed{5934}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 69 and 86, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\quad 69 \\\\\n   \\times 86 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     \\quad 414 \\quad (\\text{69 \u00d7 6}) \\\\\n   + 5520 \\quad (\\text{69 \u00d7 80, shifted one position left}) \\\\\n   \\hline\n     5934 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Distributive Property:**\n   \\[\n   69 \\times 86 = (70 - 1)(80 + 6) = 70 \\times 80 + 70 \\times 6 - 1 \\times 80 - 1 \\times 6\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 5600 + 420 - 80 - 6 = 5600 + 420 = 6020 \\quad \\text{(then subtract 86)} \\quad 6020 - 86 = 5934\n   \\]\n\n3. **Breaking Down into Smaller Parts:**\n   \\[\n   69 \\times 86 = (60 + 9)(80 + 6) = 60 \\times 80 + 60 \\times 6 + 9 \\times 80 + 9 \\times 6\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 4800 + 360 + 720 + 54 = 4800 + 360 = 5160 \\quad \\text{(then add 720 and 54)} \\quad 5160 + 720 + 54 = 5934\n   \\]\n\n4. **Verification via Estimation:**\n   \\[\n   70 \\times 85 = 5950 \\quad \\text{(approximating 69 as 70 and 86 as 85)}\n   \\]\n   Adjusting for the difference:\n   \\[\n   (70 - 1)(85 + 1) = 70 \\times 86 - 86 = 6020 - 86 = 5934\n   \\]\n\nAll methods consistently yield the result \\(5934\\).\n\n### Final Answer\nThe product of 69 and 86 is \\boxed{5934}.",
