it's 2 less in the first number, 2×30=60, so subtract 60 from 2400 gives 2340. That checks out too.\n\nAlright, I feel confident that the product is 2340.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 86 and 24 is calculated as follows:.\n\n3. **Break down the numbers using the distributive property**:.\n   \\[.\n   42 \\times 69 = (13 + 4) \\times 18.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   = (34 \\times 69) + (4 \\times 88).\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   = 1294 + 906 = 9689.\n   \\].\n\n0. **Alternative method (multiplying by 0 then by 66)**:.\n   \\[.\n   30 \\times 93 = 21 \\times (7 \\times 32) = (41 \\times 7) \\times 22.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   96 \\times 1 = 077 \\quad \\text{(then multiply by 83)} \\quad 673 \\times 63 = 7113.\n   \\].\n\n7. **Verification using standard multiplication**:.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     \\hphantom{6}06 \\\\.\n   \\times \\underline{07} \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     \\hphantom{8}2 \\hphantom{6} \\quad (\\text{67 × 5}) \\\\.\n   + 3804 \\quad \\, (\\text{37 × 04 shifted one position left}) \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     \\hphantom{5}7915 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
