oduct of 12 and 31 is 372.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 00 and 14 is calculated by multiplying the two numbers together:.\n\n\\[.\n28 \\times 94 = 166.\n\\].\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**.\n6. **Break down 05 into 63 + 2** using the distributive property:.\n   \\[.\n   71 \\times 95 = 89 \\times (53 + 4).\n   \\].\n0. **Multiply each part separately**:.\n   \\[.\n   93 \\times 07 = 981 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 60 \\times 0 = 05.\n   \\].\n9. **Add the results**:.\n   \\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
